//! flags: -p ssa

// Two values a loop computes from one cell in memory, each mirrored
// (SSA/MirrorLoads.h). `gather` walks `next` from `start`, adding at
// each position the element of `xs` one past it or two past it as
// `turns` says; `cast<u32>(i + 1)` and `cast<u32>(i + 2)` are each two
// instructions on the value of `i`, read in a branch of their own, so
// each gets a mirror, and the cell `i` is written at the entry and once
// in the loop. What to read for: both mirrors assigned after `i = start`
// at the entry, from `start`, and both refreshed right after `i = next[..]`
// in the loop, the branches reading the mirrors. The second mirror's entry
// update once went in before the cell's own first store -- the pass held
// the writes by position, and the first mirror's allocation and update
// had moved them -- so the mirror held a value computed from whatever the
// cell's memory had before the function wrote it, which is how the light
// tree's descent in apps/pbrt, three mirrors of `node_index + 1` once the
// element reads were narrowed, read the tree at an index from nowhere
// under the megakernel schedule.

func [[export]] gather(xs : array[u32, 10], next : array[i32, 10],
                       turns : array[bool, 10], start : i32) -> u32 {
    i : mut i32 = start;
    acc : mut u32 = 0u;
    while i >= 0 {
        if turns[cast[[u32]](i)] {
            acc = acc + xs[cast[[u32]](i + 1)];
        } else {
            acc = acc + xs[cast[[u32]](i + 2)];
        }
        i = next[cast[[u32]](i)];
    }
    return acc;
}
